1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:18,000
Well, we made it here. Now, to decide how we're gonna track down my dad.

2
00:00:18,000 --> 00:00:21,000
Best place to start is at the Guildhall.

3
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:35,000
Okay, fastest way to find them is to ask people about them by name.

4
00:00:35,000 --> 00:00:37,000
You think people will know their names?

5
00:00:37,000 --> 00:00:40,000
Geese likes to build an intelligence network anywhere he travels.

6
00:00:40,000 --> 00:00:47,000
We could use his name to go poking around, but unless my eyes deceive me, we needn't bother.

7
00:00:47,000 --> 00:00:49,000
We could really use you.

8
00:00:49,000 --> 00:00:52,000
Come on, big man little balls!

9
00:00:52,000 --> 00:00:54,000
Hey, Geese!

10
00:00:54,000 --> 00:00:57,000
Oh! Alina-Lise, you're here!

11
00:00:57,000 --> 00:00:59,000
Sorry it took so long.

12
00:00:59,000 --> 00:01:02,000
You kidding me? If anything, you got here fast.

13
00:01:02,000 --> 00:01:06,000
I mean, what? I only sent that letter six months ago.

14
00:01:06,000 --> 00:01:09,000
Oh, maybe you haven't seen the damn thing yet.

15
00:01:09,000 --> 00:01:11,000
We can go over all that later.

16
00:01:11,000 --> 00:01:14,000
Have any updates on Zenith's rescue?

17
00:01:14,000 --> 00:01:17,000
If I'm being honest, nothing good.

18
00:01:17,000 --> 00:01:21,000
But, no, we can go over those details later as well.

19
00:01:21,000 --> 00:01:25,000
For the moment though, would you mind taking us to see my dad?

20
00:01:25,000 --> 00:01:28,000
Sure. Whoa! Is that really you, boss man?

21
00:01:28,000 --> 00:01:31,000
You're damn near as tall as I am now.

22
00:01:31,000 --> 00:01:33,000
And you haven't changed a bit, old friend.

23
00:01:33,000 --> 00:01:37,000
Quit it. You're freaking me out. Talk down to me like you used to.

24
00:01:37,000 --> 00:01:40,000
My, you two certainly seem well acquainted.

25
00:01:40,000 --> 00:01:45,000
Yes, ma'am. We did a bit of time together behind bars. Ain't that right, boss?

26
00:01:45,000 --> 00:01:48,000
Yeah, that takes me back.

27
00:01:48,000 --> 00:01:51,000
Well, that's probably enough reminiscing for now.

28
00:01:51,000 --> 00:01:56,000
If it's Paul you want to see, come on, I'll take ya.

29
00:01:56,000 --> 00:01:58,000
See you in this interview.

30
00:01:58,000 --> 00:01:59,000
I'm following a short break.

31
00:01:59,000 --> 00:02:01,000
Meet Yab проц, one Dia.

32
00:02:01,000 --> 00:02:02,000
See you next week.

33
00:02:02,000 --> 00:02:03,000
Verse 3

34
00:02:03,000 --> 00:02:05,000
살�ei.

35
00:02:05,000 --> 00:02:06,000
I need to hang up.

36
00:02:06,000 --> 00:02:07,000
You've got to go ahead and hold the baby.

37
00:02:07,000 --> 00:02:08,000
I had 열.

38
00:02:08,000 --> 00:02:09,000
This one you got into, and if you don't fall,

39
00:02:09,000 --> 00:02:17,200
you need to be on top left after two hands or in

40
00:03:25,980 --> 00:03:33,360
Listen, Paul's been in pretty rough shape lately.

41
00:03:34,140 --> 00:03:37,580
Knowing your history, I'm sure you've got choice words for him.

42
00:03:37,840 --> 00:03:40,040
But go easy on the poor guy, if you can.

43
00:03:40,700 --> 00:03:42,380
I can try, but no promises.

44
00:03:43,920 --> 00:03:47,700
That goes for you too. Don't go startin' fights like last time.

45
00:03:48,260 --> 00:03:48,620
Right.

46
00:03:55,980 --> 00:04:01,100
Wake up, my lord. Master Rudeus has arrived.

47
00:04:08,020 --> 00:04:11,340
Is that you? You sure I'm not dreaming?

48
00:04:11,900 --> 00:04:15,400
I'm the real deal. Hey, it's been a long time.

49
00:04:16,460 --> 00:04:19,080
You actually came. Quick, too.

50
00:04:19,820 --> 00:04:22,340
Yeah, we took kind of an unusual route here.

51
00:04:23,000 --> 00:04:25,180
I'll tell you more about it when we head home.

52
00:04:25,980 --> 00:04:29,740
Well, knowing my gifted son, I shouldn't be surprised.

53
00:04:37,200 --> 00:04:42,000
Rudy, I'm so sorry. Your old man failed.

54
00:04:43,240 --> 00:04:45,020
Turns out, I can't save your mom.

55
00:04:45,700 --> 00:04:47,160
I can't keep my word.

56
00:04:47,840 --> 00:04:50,540
I just... I can't be who you need me to be.

57
00:04:51,400 --> 00:04:52,100
I'm hopeless.

58
00:04:52,100 --> 00:04:52,300
I'm hopeless.

59
00:04:52,300 --> 00:04:56,820
I'm glad I came.

60
00:04:57,760 --> 00:05:00,920
With the state Paul's in, me just being here will help.

61
00:05:02,460 --> 00:05:03,620
It's gonna be okay.

62
00:05:04,340 --> 00:05:06,840
We're together now, and we're gonna figure this out.

63
00:05:07,800 --> 00:05:08,640
Look at you.

64
00:05:09,400 --> 00:05:11,220
My boy, you're becoming a man.

65
00:05:11,780 --> 00:05:13,140
Oh, yeah, on that note,

66
00:05:13,640 --> 00:05:15,620
I'll have a child of my own soon.

67
00:05:16,060 --> 00:05:16,460
Surprise!

68
00:05:16,460 --> 00:05:18,340
Now, try and rest up.

69
00:05:18,680 --> 00:05:19,740
I can handle it from here.

70
00:05:20,780 --> 00:05:21,620
A kid?

71
00:05:23,000 --> 00:05:25,840
Rudy, you really have grown so much.

72
00:05:26,880 --> 00:05:27,360
Sorry.

73
00:05:28,360 --> 00:05:30,380
I wish I set a better example for you.

74
00:05:32,860 --> 00:05:35,200
I used to think he was larger than life,

75
00:05:36,000 --> 00:05:37,740
but now he seems so small.

76
00:05:37,740 --> 00:05:47,520
And as you can see,

77
00:05:48,100 --> 00:05:50,300
Alina Lise came with me to help search for mom.

78
00:05:50,780 --> 00:05:53,740
I know you guys didn't exactly part ways on good terms or anything.

79
00:06:03,880 --> 00:06:05,520
Alina Lise, I...

80
00:06:05,520 --> 00:06:06,700
The hell do you want?

81
00:06:06,700 --> 00:06:14,760
I'm sorry for what I did.

82
00:06:20,040 --> 00:06:21,460
I share some blame.

83
00:06:21,800 --> 00:06:23,300
You know, maybe a small part.

84
00:06:23,300 --> 00:06:35,820
Thank you, friend.

85
00:06:36,080 --> 00:06:36,940
I owe you.

86
00:06:37,760 --> 00:06:38,820
No, old friend.

87
00:06:39,200 --> 00:06:39,920
You don't.

88
00:06:39,920 --> 00:06:50,860
Don't tell me you missed me so much you did it with my son.

89
00:06:50,940 --> 00:06:52,040
Of course I didn't.

90
00:06:52,380 --> 00:06:54,620
Cliff's invention keeps my impulses at bay.

91
00:06:54,620 --> 00:06:56,900
Oh, first I'm hearing of this Cliff fella.

92
00:06:56,920 --> 00:06:57,680
He's my husband.

93
00:06:57,900 --> 00:06:58,920
You wouldn't know him.

94
00:06:59,120 --> 00:06:59,500
Huh?

95
00:06:59,500 --> 00:07:01,140
This a joke?

96
00:07:01,640 --> 00:07:03,340
We'd be crazy enough to marry you.

97
00:07:04,140 --> 00:07:06,020
I mean, you gotta be kidding me.

98
00:07:06,280 --> 00:07:07,800
You're taking it a little far, Dad.

99
00:07:08,380 --> 00:07:10,940
He's respectable and he happens to be my friend too.

100
00:07:11,240 --> 00:07:12,820
That you don't say.

101
00:07:13,640 --> 00:07:14,080
All right.

102
00:07:14,140 --> 00:07:15,120
I'm sorry about that.

103
00:07:15,340 --> 00:07:16,580
I'd love to meet him one day.

104
00:07:16,880 --> 00:07:17,520
Oh, good.

105
00:07:17,880 --> 00:07:20,180
Then you can see what a real man is like, Paul.

106
00:07:20,880 --> 00:07:21,360
Anyway.

107
00:07:22,020 --> 00:07:24,500
Rudeus, Alina Lys, thank you.

108
00:07:24,960 --> 00:07:26,060
I'm glad you're both here.

109
00:07:27,040 --> 00:07:28,660
Isn't that what family is for?

110
00:07:28,860 --> 00:07:30,840
Save your thanks for what comes next.

111
00:07:31,200 --> 00:07:31,500
Hmm.

112
00:07:33,380 --> 00:07:34,880
Let's get you both caught up.

113
00:07:36,440 --> 00:07:39,460
According to Geese's intel, if it holds true,

114
00:07:39,920 --> 00:07:42,940
Zenith is trapped in a labyrinth a day's journey north of here.

115
00:07:44,680 --> 00:07:46,840
She's been in there for six whole years?

116
00:07:47,120 --> 00:07:47,720
Can't say.

117
00:07:48,300 --> 00:07:49,480
Is her life in danger?

118
00:07:49,480 --> 00:07:51,820
Can't say.

119
00:07:52,920 --> 00:07:53,360
Hmm.

120
00:07:53,780 --> 00:07:58,580
Rumor has it, a young woman matching Zenith's description was a party member with some group

121
00:07:58,580 --> 00:08:00,740
that went missing in there a few years back.

122
00:08:01,060 --> 00:08:05,800
It sounds like she's been spotted in there again more recently, but that's all we have to go off.

123
00:08:06,320 --> 00:08:09,120
This is an old labyrinth and a dangerous one at that.

124
00:08:09,800 --> 00:08:15,500
Case in point, our group with four professionals has taken a year to barely make it halfway in sign.

125
00:08:16,440 --> 00:08:17,840
Pretty pathetic, huh?

126
00:08:19,480 --> 00:08:25,060
Oh, seems we've got some visitors.

127
00:08:25,920 --> 00:08:28,620
Now I'd wager that you're Paul's boy, am I right?

128
00:08:28,980 --> 00:08:29,880
That's me, yeah.

129
00:08:30,400 --> 00:08:31,460
It's nice to meet you.

130
00:08:31,560 --> 00:08:32,460
My name's Rudeus.

131
00:08:32,820 --> 00:08:34,120
And I am Talhand.

132
00:08:34,120 --> 00:08:38,400
If I may say, you look just as brilliant as I've heard you are.

133
00:08:39,000 --> 00:08:40,180
And then some.

134
00:08:41,180 --> 00:08:44,400
Now that everyone's here, let's pick up where we left off.

135
00:08:44,740 --> 00:08:45,080
Okay?

136
00:08:45,740 --> 00:08:46,040
Wait.

137
00:08:46,600 --> 00:08:47,060
Everyone?

138
00:08:47,680 --> 00:08:48,280
Hang on.

139
00:08:48,660 --> 00:08:49,400
Who's everyone?

140
00:08:50,060 --> 00:08:51,620
Shouldn't we wait for Master Roxy?

141
00:08:51,620 --> 00:08:55,940
No.

142
00:08:57,060 --> 00:08:58,120
You don't meet.

143
00:08:59,120 --> 00:09:03,060
About a month ago, she fell into a trap down there.

144
00:09:05,160 --> 00:09:06,300
She's not dead.

145
00:09:07,120 --> 00:09:07,520
Is she?

146
00:09:07,520 --> 00:09:10,160
She can't be.

147
00:09:10,700 --> 00:09:12,520
She's a king-class water mage.

148
00:09:13,040 --> 00:09:14,980
She's taken on labyrinths alone before.

149
00:09:16,440 --> 00:09:17,380
Don't say it.

150
00:09:18,020 --> 00:09:18,360
Please.

151
00:09:18,760 --> 00:09:19,540
I don't want to know.

152
00:09:19,540 --> 00:09:19,600
No.

153
00:09:21,800 --> 00:09:25,260
She just stepped on a teleportation circle and went missing.

154
00:09:25,820 --> 00:09:27,600
So we can't assume she's dead yet.

155
00:09:27,600 --> 00:09:29,980
Paul, don't give him false hope.

156
00:09:30,360 --> 00:09:32,640
A magician ain't gonna make it out of there alive.

157
00:09:32,900 --> 00:09:33,240
Maybe.

158
00:09:33,620 --> 00:09:35,600
But Roxy is an exceptional magician.

159
00:09:36,320 --> 00:09:38,660
There's a better than good chance she's still kicking.

160
00:09:39,400 --> 00:09:41,020
She's been gone a whole month.

161
00:09:41,160 --> 00:09:42,260
You think she's alive?

162
00:09:42,520 --> 00:09:45,360
We went down there five times and came back empty-handed.

163
00:09:45,780 --> 00:09:48,240
Geese, how long are you gonna keep up the charade?

164
00:09:48,240 --> 00:09:57,780
Sorry to interrupt.

165
00:09:58,320 --> 00:10:00,180
I didn't mean to derail the whole meeting.

166
00:10:00,960 --> 00:10:03,780
I know it's a labyrinth, but what are we getting into?

167
00:10:05,060 --> 00:10:06,860
One of the worst dives around.

168
00:10:07,460 --> 00:10:08,880
The damn thing's S-ranked.

169
00:10:08,940 --> 00:10:09,900
It's brutal in there.

170
00:10:10,960 --> 00:10:12,800
It's a teleporter labyrinth.

171
00:10:14,880 --> 00:10:16,740
Wait, I have something that might help.

172
00:10:18,240 --> 00:10:20,900
It's a journal.

173
00:10:21,360 --> 00:10:24,900
An official account by an adventurer who made it pretty deep into that labyrinth.

174
00:10:25,600 --> 00:10:26,800
You think you guys could use it?

175
00:10:27,620 --> 00:10:29,140
How the hell did you get this?

176
00:10:29,520 --> 00:10:30,800
I borrowed it from the university.

177
00:10:31,660 --> 00:10:33,400
Hey, Geese, look it over, will ya?

178
00:10:34,400 --> 00:10:35,240
Sure thing.

179
00:10:35,460 --> 00:10:36,340
What do we got here?

180
00:10:36,340 --> 00:10:49,760
That's my boss for ya!

181
00:10:49,960 --> 00:10:52,460
If what's written in these pages is actually correct,

182
00:10:52,740 --> 00:10:55,200
we've as good as made it to the sixth stratum now!

183
00:10:55,560 --> 00:10:56,080
You sure?

184
00:10:56,080 --> 00:10:58,920
Yeah, it fills in all the intel gaps we're missing!

185
00:11:00,860 --> 00:11:03,420
Okay, everyone come take a look.

186
00:11:03,740 --> 00:11:05,320
Then we'll knock out our formation.

187
00:11:05,660 --> 00:11:05,920
Alright!

188
00:11:06,360 --> 00:11:06,720
Okay!

189
00:11:06,720 --> 00:11:14,800
This is our first time sharing sleeping quarters, isn't it, my lord?

190
00:11:15,220 --> 00:11:16,260
I suppose so.

191
00:11:16,940 --> 00:11:20,700
Please don't hesitate to complain if your lord father's snoring disturbs you.

192
00:11:21,140 --> 00:11:22,300
Oh, I won't.

193
00:11:23,260 --> 00:11:24,600
And Master Rudeus?

194
00:11:25,220 --> 00:11:26,260
Yeah, what do you need?

195
00:11:26,660 --> 00:11:29,300
Is Aisha performing her duties to your liking?

196
00:11:29,960 --> 00:11:31,880
Yeah, she's a hard worker.

197
00:11:31,880 --> 00:11:36,360
I know she can be a handful, but she hasn't caused you any trouble, right?

198
00:11:37,060 --> 00:11:38,000
No, not a bit.

199
00:11:38,520 --> 00:11:39,960
She's been doing all the chores.

200
00:11:40,420 --> 00:11:41,620
We'd be lost without her.

201
00:11:42,100 --> 00:11:43,040
Oh, is that so?

202
00:11:43,740 --> 00:11:45,920
Well, I hope she isn't being too selfish.

203
00:11:46,660 --> 00:11:51,700
She's not, but sometimes I feel like things would actually be a lot easier if she was more demanding.

204
00:11:54,800 --> 00:11:55,880
What's with that look?

205
00:11:56,420 --> 00:11:58,180
You've been smirking for a while now.

206
00:11:58,180 --> 00:11:59,000
Oh, nothing.

207
00:11:59,320 --> 00:12:01,380
Just thinking about how nice this is.

208
00:12:01,880 --> 00:12:02,640
How nice what is?

209
00:12:03,340 --> 00:12:04,560
My boy growing up.

210
00:12:05,080 --> 00:12:06,140
Sitting around.

211
00:12:07,040 --> 00:12:08,980
Having a lovely conversation with Lelia.

212
00:12:10,000 --> 00:12:11,340
Which reminds me.

213
00:12:11,720 --> 00:12:13,980
You mentioned you got a kid on the way, didn't you?

214
00:12:14,260 --> 00:12:14,840
I do.

215
00:12:15,620 --> 00:12:18,300
Honestly, we have a lot to catch up on.

216
00:12:18,840 --> 00:12:19,560
I got married.

217
00:12:20,700 --> 00:12:21,160
Oh, yeah?

218
00:12:21,780 --> 00:12:22,300
To who?

219
00:12:22,900 --> 00:12:24,380
Wait, heiress, right?

220
00:12:24,540 --> 00:12:25,940
No, to Sylphiette.

221
00:12:26,460 --> 00:12:28,520
We reunited at the university.

222
00:12:29,420 --> 00:12:29,960
Sylphie?

223
00:12:30,280 --> 00:12:31,440
The girl from Buena?

224
00:12:31,880 --> 00:12:33,040
She made it?

225
00:12:33,540 --> 00:12:34,020
She did.

226
00:12:34,660 --> 00:12:37,460
But she had it rough, just like everyone else who survived.

227
00:12:38,980 --> 00:12:40,120
You don't say.

228
00:12:41,060 --> 00:12:41,620
Marriage.

229
00:12:42,440 --> 00:12:43,160
And a kid.

230
00:12:44,180 --> 00:12:45,080
My grandkid.

231
00:12:45,080 --> 00:12:45,140
My grandkid.

232
00:12:45,140 --> 00:12:49,880
Sorry for all of this.

233
00:12:49,880 --> 00:12:55,480
If I wasn't so damn useless, I would not have dragged you out here when you're about to be a father.

234
00:12:56,280 --> 00:12:57,060
Oh, it's okay.

235
00:12:57,940 --> 00:12:59,320
It shouldn't all be on you.

236
00:13:00,160 --> 00:13:02,740
I'm sorry for doing my own thing when mom is still missing.

237
00:13:02,740 --> 00:13:05,480
Don't be.

238
00:13:05,900 --> 00:13:08,320
And how about you host the party when we get home?

239
00:13:09,880 --> 00:13:10,320
Yes.

240
00:13:11,520 --> 00:13:14,060
And we gotta go big with this baby on the way.

241
00:13:14,300 --> 00:13:15,700
You're gonna beat Grand Paul.

242
00:13:15,700 --> 00:13:17,060
Hey, watch it, kid.

243
00:13:17,540 --> 00:13:19,260
I don't need to be reminded of my age.

244
00:13:20,360 --> 00:13:25,100
Now, since you've got a little one on the way, I'm guessing you've officially become a man.

245
00:13:25,660 --> 00:13:26,640
Heavens, my lord.

246
00:13:27,080 --> 00:13:30,200
I'm not sure this line of vulgar questioning is appropriate, sir.

247
00:13:30,640 --> 00:13:31,620
Oh, come on.

248
00:13:31,700 --> 00:13:32,580
He's my son.

249
00:13:33,080 --> 00:13:36,100
I'd like to have these talks with him at least once in his life.

250
00:13:36,360 --> 00:13:40,940
And besides, your old man likes to think he's a bit of an expert in marital relations.

251
00:13:41,220 --> 00:13:42,700
So, ask me anything.

252
00:13:43,360 --> 00:13:44,180
Okay, then.

253
00:13:44,600 --> 00:13:47,120
I do have a few questions I'd like to ask you.

254
00:13:47,440 --> 00:13:49,820
Please don't encourage your father, Master Rudeus.

255
00:13:50,500 --> 00:13:52,320
Oh, don't let her fool you, son.

256
00:13:52,320 --> 00:13:54,940
You get that dress offer and she goes buck wild.

257
00:13:55,080 --> 00:13:55,920
Master Paul!

258
00:13:56,520 --> 00:13:57,160
Oh, yeah.

259
00:13:57,500 --> 00:13:59,980
Come to think of it, she's the one that came on to me.

260
00:13:59,980 --> 00:14:01,640
That fateful, sweaty night.

261
00:14:02,440 --> 00:14:02,920
Fascinating.

262
00:14:03,300 --> 00:14:04,500
Please, tell me more.

263
00:14:04,580 --> 00:14:07,100
Master Rudeus, stop it, both of you.

264
00:14:12,260 --> 00:14:14,660
Rudy, make sure you stick to the plan.

265
00:14:14,920 --> 00:14:15,400
You got it?

266
00:14:15,900 --> 00:14:16,420
Yes, sir.

267
00:14:17,140 --> 00:14:17,800
Best of luck.

268
00:14:18,520 --> 00:14:19,160
All of you.

269
00:14:21,000 --> 00:14:21,480
Right.

270
00:14:22,100 --> 00:14:22,640
Move out.

271
00:14:27,980 --> 00:14:29,300
Would you look at that?

272
00:14:29,300 --> 00:14:32,340
All your boy's got some handy tricks up his sleeves.

273
00:14:33,120 --> 00:14:33,840
Oh, I know.

274
00:14:34,120 --> 00:14:35,800
Proud to call him my son for a reason.

275
00:14:37,960 --> 00:14:39,540
Am I remembering this correctly?

276
00:14:39,840 --> 00:14:44,020
The circles will teleport you somewhere if you step on one, so walk around them, but not

277
00:14:44,020 --> 00:14:46,320
all of them glow, so keep your eyes peeled.

278
00:14:46,600 --> 00:14:47,580
Or something like that?

279
00:14:48,140 --> 00:14:48,740
That's right.

280
00:14:49,200 --> 00:14:52,240
The best way to avoid a slip-up is to step where Geese does.

281
00:14:52,240 --> 00:14:55,900
A monster!

282
00:14:55,900 --> 00:14:56,060
A monster!

283
00:15:11,060 --> 00:15:11,660
What?

284
00:15:11,660 --> 00:15:14,420
I can wipe the floor with those all day long.

285
00:15:16,820 --> 00:15:17,740
Piece of cake.

286
00:15:17,960 --> 00:15:18,620
Bring it on.

287
00:15:21,200 --> 00:15:21,600
Hm.

288
00:15:21,600 --> 00:15:23,540
Oh, boy.

289
00:15:24,160 --> 00:15:25,840
I bet he's trying to show off for me.

290
00:15:26,420 --> 00:15:27,900
Yeah, yeah, you're a cool warrior.

291
00:15:28,140 --> 00:15:29,260
I see you.

292
00:15:29,500 --> 00:15:31,360
Just don't get sloppy, old man.

293
00:15:31,600 --> 00:15:32,520
Slow down.

294
00:15:32,900 --> 00:15:35,080
You keep pushing too far ahead of me, Paul.

295
00:15:35,240 --> 00:15:36,360
This isn't the plan.

296
00:15:37,080 --> 00:15:38,480
We're still in the first stratum.

297
00:15:38,540 --> 00:15:39,640
It's not that big a deal.

298
00:15:39,860 --> 00:15:41,340
Not to us it isn't.

299
00:15:41,460 --> 00:15:44,080
But this is your son's first time in a labyrinth.

300
00:15:44,260 --> 00:15:44,940
You're an adult.

301
00:15:45,080 --> 00:15:45,840
Act like one.

302
00:15:46,180 --> 00:15:50,140
I'm just pulling ahead so I can strike up a conversation with him and try to loosen

303
00:15:50,140 --> 00:15:50,960
his nerves a bit.

304
00:15:51,040 --> 00:15:52,220
Oh, cut the crap.

305
00:15:52,640 --> 00:15:53,780
You're doing that for you.

306
00:15:54,180 --> 00:15:58,160
I think the last time I saw you this giddy, you just roped Zenith into the party.

307
00:15:58,620 --> 00:16:01,960
When you put it that way, I guess I can't really argue with you.

308
00:16:02,460 --> 00:16:03,640
What's gotten into you?

309
00:16:03,820 --> 00:16:06,080
I don't remember you being this much of a nag.

310
00:16:06,080 --> 00:16:07,420
Are you kidding me?

311
00:16:07,780 --> 00:16:10,160
You're practically a son to me now.

312
00:16:10,300 --> 00:16:11,640
I'll nag all I want.

313
00:16:11,980 --> 00:16:13,640
How the hell would I be your son?

314
00:16:14,100 --> 00:16:14,740
Right, Rudy?

315
00:16:17,700 --> 00:16:18,640
Sorry, Paul.

316
00:16:18,720 --> 00:16:19,280
It's true.

317
00:16:19,420 --> 00:16:20,180
You're in-laws.

318
00:16:20,740 --> 00:16:21,460
Sort of.

319
00:16:25,240 --> 00:16:28,200
That circle over there leads to the second stratum.

320
00:16:29,160 --> 00:16:30,520
I'll need to clear out the bugs.

321
00:16:30,960 --> 00:16:31,440
Let's go.

322
00:16:32,880 --> 00:16:34,800
Remember, don't use fire.

323
00:16:34,800 --> 00:16:36,160
No, why not?

324
00:16:36,500 --> 00:16:40,180
When you cast fire in a closed space, it fills the air with poison.

325
00:16:40,520 --> 00:16:43,280
The deeper you go, the more careful you're going to have to be.

326
00:16:44,480 --> 00:16:47,920
By poison, I'm guessing he's referring to carbon monoxide.

327
00:16:47,920 --> 00:16:50,260
No fire.

328
00:16:50,260 --> 00:16:52,400
And no attacking the ceiling, either.

329
00:16:52,640 --> 00:16:54,560
You can probably guess why.

330
00:16:55,380 --> 00:16:57,300
Because it might trigger a cave-in, right?

331
00:16:57,680 --> 00:16:57,980
Right.

332
00:16:58,440 --> 00:17:00,540
Same reason you don't use much water, either.

333
00:17:01,280 --> 00:17:02,660
You don't want to stick with ice.

334
00:17:03,560 --> 00:17:04,100
Got it.

335
00:17:04,100 --> 00:17:14,480
I can see you learn from Ratsy.

336
00:17:14,700 --> 00:17:16,700
You even cast some of the same spells.

337
00:17:22,700 --> 00:17:24,640
This one should be safe.

338
00:17:24,640 --> 00:17:25,560
All right.

339
00:17:25,880 --> 00:17:27,320
Everyone, step onto the circle.

340
00:17:38,060 --> 00:17:38,580
Okay.

341
00:17:39,100 --> 00:17:40,440
Let's take a quick breather.

342
00:17:40,440 --> 00:17:46,720
Hey, Rudy.

343
00:17:47,500 --> 00:17:48,960
You'd better rest up, son.

344
00:17:49,240 --> 00:17:49,660
Sorry.

345
00:17:49,860 --> 00:17:50,240
Yes, sir.

346
00:17:51,920 --> 00:17:53,660
Paul's starting to distance himself.

347
00:17:54,340 --> 00:17:58,140
He checked on me during every break in the first stratum, but now...

348
00:17:58,140 --> 00:17:59,280
He's getting pretty quiet.

349
00:17:59,280 --> 00:18:02,120
I guess it's to be expected.

350
00:18:02,520 --> 00:18:03,880
Second stratum, more focus.

351
00:18:04,700 --> 00:18:06,240
The ghoul dad's so serious.

352
00:18:06,480 --> 00:18:07,200
All right, boss.

353
00:18:07,420 --> 00:18:09,000
We're coming up on the third stratum.

354
00:18:09,300 --> 00:18:13,640
If your book is telling the truth, traps only send you to another part of the same floor.

355
00:18:14,220 --> 00:18:17,400
If we're lucky, Ratsy might still be holed up down there somewhere.

356
00:18:17,920 --> 00:18:18,220
Great.

357
00:18:22,140 --> 00:18:25,100
I thought it would take us several days to delve this far.

358
00:18:26,060 --> 00:18:27,000
Normally would.

359
00:18:27,000 --> 00:18:29,760
But this time, we've got your fancy book as a guide.

360
00:18:30,820 --> 00:18:34,900
Shouldn't surprise me that having a map versus going in blind makes a big difference.

361
00:18:35,640 --> 00:18:37,420
But now the real challenge begins.

362
00:18:37,940 --> 00:18:39,300
We have to find Ratsy.

363
00:18:40,320 --> 00:18:41,500
Hey, boss man.

364
00:18:41,700 --> 00:18:44,620
Based on your intuition, where do you think Ratsy's hiding out?

365
00:18:45,360 --> 00:18:46,360
My intuition?

366
00:18:57,000 --> 00:19:01,580
What's wrong, young one?

367
00:19:02,360 --> 00:19:02,620
Rudy?

368
00:19:03,460 --> 00:19:04,320
What is it?

369
00:19:04,320 --> 00:19:15,380
What's come over you all of a sudden?

370
00:19:15,380 --> 00:19:15,440
What's come over you all of a sudden?

371
00:19:15,440 --> 00:19:26,800
Sheep me in the Earth's magnificent armor.

372
00:19:28,020 --> 00:19:28,980
Earth's fortress!

373
00:19:33,500 --> 00:19:37,200
Scatter the fallen droplets and blanket the world in water.

374
00:19:38,080 --> 00:19:39,320
Water splash!

375
00:19:39,320 --> 00:19:46,800
As her goddess in the fields of heaven, swing thy staff and cover this world in frost.

376
00:19:47,020 --> 00:19:48,160
Icicle field!

377
00:19:50,680 --> 00:19:53,720
O king of frost, glacial lord who governs death.

378
00:19:54,060 --> 00:19:57,360
Sovereign in white and supreme ruler of the Arctic lands.

379
00:19:57,760 --> 00:19:59,940
Freeze thy enemy, break the world of its heat.

380
00:20:01,000 --> 00:20:02,180
Blizzard storm!

381
00:20:02,180 --> 00:20:23,680
Not good enough.

382
00:20:24,340 --> 00:20:25,040
Not figures.

383
00:20:25,040 --> 00:20:25,260
Not figures.

384
00:20:25,260 --> 00:20:35,780
Take up thy scorching blade and cleave my foes.

385
00:20:36,120 --> 00:20:37,140
Flame slice!

386
00:20:39,980 --> 00:20:42,400
Sheep me in the Earth's magnificent armor.

387
00:20:42,940 --> 00:20:43,820
Earth's fortress.

388
00:20:50,820 --> 00:20:51,460
No.

389
00:20:54,180 --> 00:20:54,780
No!

390
00:20:55,260 --> 00:21:04,460
I don't want to die.

391
00:21:05,340 --> 00:21:07,940
Someone, please, help.

392
00:21:08,940 --> 00:21:09,620
Anyone?

393
00:21:11,000 --> 00:21:13,440
Save me.

394
00:21:13,440 --> 00:21:13,480
Save me.

395
00:21:18,120 --> 00:21:18,900
Huh?

396
00:21:19,140 --> 00:21:45,300
Oh, my God.

397
00:21:45,460 --> 00:21:45,640
Please.

398
00:21:46,180 --> 00:21:47,400
Oh.

399
00:21:47,400 --> 00:21:51,960
Thank goodness.

400
00:23:35,980 --> 00:23:39,980
La-ya-la-ya-la

